1. Definitions

1.1 "UniVex Studios" means UniVex Studios, the copyright owner and licensor of
    the Software.

1.2 "You" (and "your") means the individual or legal entity exercising rights
    under this Agreement.

1.3 "Source Code" means the human-readable source files, build scripts,
    shaders, and configuration files included with the Software.

1.4 "End-User Product" means a video game, interactive simulation,
    visualization, or other application built by you with the Software that
    delivers substantial original content or functionality of your own and is
    not itself a general-purpose game engine, editor, SDK, or authoring tool.

1.5 "Runtime Components" means the compiled runtime binaries, supporting
    runtime libraries, and built-in shader assets of the Software (such as the
    UniVex runtime executable and its required runtime libraries) strictly
    needed to run an End-User Product.


