3. Restrictions

The Software is source-available, not open-source. Unless expressly allowed
under Section 2 or in a separate written agreement signed by UniVex Studios,
you may not:

(a) redistribute, sell, lease, sublicense, mirror, or publish the Software,
    the Source Code, UniVex Editor, UniVex Hub, build tools (including UVBT),
    or any modified version or fork as a standalone product, SDK, engine
    distribution, editor, or competing development tool;

(b) rebrand, white-label, or present the Software (whether modified or
    unmodified) as your own engine or editor, or as another third-party
    engine;

(c) distribute standalone Runtime Components, or allow end users to extract or
    reuse Runtime Components to build or run unrelated third-party products;

(d) remove, hide, or alter any copyright notices, license files, or
    third-party attributions included with the Software; or

(e) use the Software in violation of applicable law or third-party rights.


